// Regression test: forces the switch's interned constant vector to begin at
// a pool index exceeding u8, requiring the wide multiway-skip encoding (see
// pkg/zkc/vm/internal/interpreter/encoding/switch.go) -- achieved by first
// interning 300 distinct (non-foldable, input-dependent) constants via a
// sequential ADD chain.  NOTE: addition is used here rather than XOR
// deliberately -- an equivalent XOR chain inflates the range-check codegen
// at small max-static-height configurations (see skip_if_06, which isolates
// that unrelated pre-existing limitation) enough to overflow the u16 skip
// bound of the general conditional-skip encoding, unrelated to the SKIP_M
// form under test here.
input inputs(c:u1) -> (d:u8)
input outputs(c:u1) -> (out:u32)

